+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates a tool input against its resolved `inputSchema`, returns a `ToolResponse` describing a rejected input, and does not invoke the executor when validation fails ([validated by: rejects malformed input before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- Valid input, including properties not declared by the schema, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input through unchanged, including an extra property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L41)).
+- Static schemas compile at registration, dynamic schemas are resolved for each call, and an uncompilable schema names its tool in the registration error ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and validates the current dynamic schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L55)).
+- A rejected tool call becomes readable tool-result content on the next model round, while an unknown tool name still throws ([validated by: feeds a validation rejection into the retry round and preserves the unknown-tool throw](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
